decompiling,
  specializing and instancing charstrings, and fix programToCommands
miscounting
  operands when several blend operators precede the first stem or moveto
(#4337,
  #4339).
- [instancer] Round CFF2 outlines and stem hints on absolute positions
rather than
  per relative operand, and keep CFF2 Private DICT blend values at full
precision
  until they are written back (#4338, #4341).
- [cffLib] Preserve CFF2 Private DICT arrays that use more than one blend
group
  (#4346).
- [feaLib] Raise FeatureLibError instead of looping forever on an unclosed
  ``OS/2``, BASE or STAT table block (#4347).
- [designspaceLib] When a variable font overrides some ``public.fontInfo``
keys,
  merge them with the root-level font info instead of replacing it (#4336,
#4340).
- [instancer] Raise an error for FeatureVariations conditions of a format
other
  than the supported axis-range one, instead of silently dropping them
(#4348).
- [filesystem] Don't overwrite an unrelated sibling ``.zip when writing a
.ufoz``
  or other non-``.zip`` archive (#4342).
- [glyf] Fix exponential running time on composite glyphs that reuse the
same
  component at several nesting levels; getCoordinates now raises TTLibError
  past 65535 composite points (#4325).
- [ttLib] Add support for the beyond-64k tables of the final ISO Open Font
Format
  5th edition: uppercase companion tables (GLYF, GVAR, HMTX, GSUB/GPOS
  extended layout, FeatureVariations 1.1, TTC 1.1/2.1, DMAP), a
  ``ttLib.beyond64k`` module and CLI, and support in FontBuilder, merge,
  subset, instancer, qu2cu, removeOverlaps and scaleUpem (#4097,
  #2678).
- [VARC] Keep ``addVarComponent()`` locations sparse, passing
RESET_UNSPECIFIED_AXES
  via a new keyword-only resetUnspecifiedAxes pen argument (#4349).
- [woff] Require brotli >= 1.2.1 and brotlicffi >= 1.2.1.0, which fix
  GHSA-9v8h-qqgm-4m35 (#4365, #4370).
- Build Windows ARM64 wheels (#4366).
- [instancer] Fix ``AttributeError: ElidedFallbackNameID`` when updating
font names of
  a font with a version 1.0 STAT table; fall back to the subfamily name
(#2933,
  #4371).

4.67.0 (released 2026-10-14)
